  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 0.619 acc, a large +9.2% jump over config_008 (same but singleprofile, no aggregation at 0.527). This shows multiprofile + avgpool is the dominant driver so far. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether avgpool is the optimal aggregation or whether a transformer aggregation would further improve multiprofile integration. Question tested: config_014 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings identical to config_003 (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat, multiprofile), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why this is the best next experiment: aggregation is the most recently introduced and highest-impact design axis; resolving whether a more expressive aggregator (transformer) helps or whether simple averaging already captures the multiprofile benefit will either open a new high-performing direction or confirm we should focus remaining budget on image encoder or fusion method. A single-variable comparison with the current best is the most information-efficient use of the next slot."
}

